> > I need to set up a daily entry in the root crontab file which will do a
> > simple backup operation, copying a directory from one location to another.
> > The trick is that the destination file will have the format 'DDMMYY' which
> > is the date that it executes.
> >                                  I have tried a few methods, the nearest I
> > got was
> >  (e.g. 'cp -R /usr/tmp /usr/tmp/`date +%A` ) which will name the destination
