> > directory)
> >       But I haven't got it in the required format (DDMMYY). Is there a
> > better way to do this?
> >      Will it involve some sort of command substitution with `date` as above?
> >
> > Regards - Tom
> 
> Try :  cp -R /usr/tmp /usr/tmp/`date +%d%m%y`
> 

... and to avoid a common mistake from last century, you should
consider using

   cp -R /usr/tmp /usr/tmp/`date +%d%m%Y`

instead. Bytes aren't that expensive anymore. If you expect to collect
many such files, you might even prefer

   cp -R /usr/tmp /usr/tmp/`date +%Y%m%d`

so the filenames can easily be sorted in chronological order.

Regards,

Timo Felbinger

