"Michael J." wrote:
> finger -f | grep -v root | cut -f 1 -d " " | kill . . . . . .

You need ps.  Here are two solutions:

All user pids:

    ps -eo pid,user | awk '! /root/ && ! /PID/ {print $1}' | xargs kill

Pids of logged-in users only:

    ps -eo pid -u `u | sed s/root//` | tail +2 | xargs kill

Note that the pids just get a sig; they may choose to ignore it, unless
you give them kurare #9.


But how about:

    init s



