Most of the stuff is tunable via the /etc/sysconfigtab file.

The sysconfig command can be used to display and modify the values.

The dxkerneltuner command can also be used to change these values in a
"point and click" X-Window interface.

The "System Configuration and Tuning" manual should be able to give you
more details on what to modify.  Start with the following URL and
select the documentation set that goes with the version of Tru64 UNIX
that you are attempting to gather information about:

