Oh, but as far as I recall, most of 433au systems can only support 
1 (one) SCSI adapter due to PCI chipset issue in early au-series. 
Therefore, this KZPBA-CA must be your one, and only SCSI adapter,
right? Further, KZPBA-CA officially supports 1 (one) SCSI connection
point, which can be either internal, or external - but NOT both at
the same time. Now, au-series come with an SCSI disk installed 
internally, so that they do *not* support externally attached SCSI
devices on the first KZPBA-CA, at least not officially. Therefore,
if it works - feel lucky. If it doesn't - well ...

The real issue with internal/external SCSI connections on KZPBA-CA
seems to be cabling length: the internal cable is already close to
the Ultra-SCSI chain limit, leaving at most two feet (and may be 
just one) for any external chains. This may be enough for one external
enclosure if you push it, but is almost guaranteed to blow it if you
have two (which is that you seem to be trying to do).

You may try to replace the internal ribbon cable with a shorter one - 
as long as you do not use all four internal bays, this should be
possible. Also, make sure that the on-card SCSI chain termination
is off (I believe that is controlled by pkc_term SRM variable).
If it still does not work ... well, it was nether supposed to.

Cheers,

/Serge.P

