>chk_bf_quota : user quota underflow on fileset.
>
>Is there is any way to avoid this message and what could be the reason ?

This is a known bug.  I do not know the status of the patch kit, but I
know that a patch for this was in the works.  Check the latest v4.0d
patch kit and see if this is addressed:

        <http://www.tru64unix.compaq.com/serv_support.html>

If the latest patch kit does not have this fix yet, then the short term
solution is to add userquota,groupquota options to your /etc/fstab
AdvFS entries (see "man 4 fstab"), and then run the quotacheck command
to clear up the problem for now.

AdvFS always maintains quotas, it just does not enforce them unless it
is asked to.  So adding userquota,groupquota to /etc/fstab will not
change what AdvFS does, it will just allow you to run quotacheck.

Until you have the patch installed, just run quotacheck when you get
the quota underflow error.



