First: check if you have your location file listed in any of the subdirs
( country directories) in the /etc/zoneinfo dir.
Once you find that,do this..
suppose: your matching timezone file is located at:
/etc/zoneinfo/US/Michigan ( which has all those daylight things working
) do this:

cd /etc/zoneinfo
mv localtime localtime.back
ln -s ./US/Michigan localtime
You are all set.
Now you need not do it on all systems, work on one and setup a NTP
server and setup NTP clients on the rest. It is a simple way. All you
need then is to ensure that the server keeps the time.

Gopi.
