You are lucky my friend in this case :)) I had an advanced level of
this problem. And I had to do this :))
My case had a strange problem, the number of pty*s didnt match t*
devices in /dev dir.. resulting in a mess.
I had a big count for npty in kernel config file during doconfig.
Resolution:
Delete all those unmatching pty* and tty* s and recreate them with
MAKEDEV PTY_1 PTY_2 ...

That solved the problem.

Also take a look at the SYSV_PTY script in /dev

Gopi.

